/**

@page peano_action_sets Action sets and traversal events

\tableofcontents

Action sets attach application behaviour to the events emitted by
peano4::topology::TreeTraversal. The Python class
exahype2.actionsets.ActionSet provides one body for each generated callback,
and an observer invokes its action sets in their configured order.

# Traversal lifecycle

Every rank starts from one observer prototype. The topology manager creates a
rank observer, and a parallel traversal creates an additional clone for each
subtree task. Clones may execute concurrently and therefore keep their mutable
state private. Static `prepareTraversal()` and `unprepareTraversal()` hooks
run once per rank around the complete sweep.

Each observer clone receives `beginTraversal()` before its first event and
`endTraversal()` after its last event. A face or vertex that two subtree tasks
hold can therefore have one first-touch and last-touch lifecycle per task
copy. The interface merge callbacks reconcile these copies with one sweep of
lag.

# Events

Event | Semantics | Ordering
----- | --------- | --------
prepareTraversal | Prepares rank-wide action-set state. | Runs before any observer instance is constructed.
beginTraversal | Starts one rank or subtree-task observer. | Precedes every entity event of that observer.
createVertex | Initialises a newly created persistent vertex. | Precedes its first touch.
createFace | Initialises a newly created face. | Follows creation of its adjacent vertices and precedes its first touch.
createCell | Initialises a newly created cell. | Follows creation of its adjacent faces and vertices and precedes its first touch.
touchHangingVertexFirstTime | Presents a hanging vertex before adjacent fine-grid work. | Precedes adjacent face and cell events.
touchHangingFaceFirstTime | Presents a hanging face before its adjacent fine-grid cell. | Follows the relevant vertex events.
touchVertexFirstTime | Presents a persistent vertex for its first use by this observer. | Precedes adjacent face and cell events.
touchFaceFirstTime | Presents a face for its first use by this observer. | Follows adjacent vertex first touches and precedes adjacent cell events.
touchCellFirstTime | Enters a cell. | Follows first touches of adjacent vertices and faces.
touchCellLastTime | Leaves a cell after its descendants. | Precedes last touches of adjacent faces and vertices.
touchFaceLastTime | Presents a face after its adjacent local cells. | Precedes destruction when the transition removes the face.
touchVertexLastTime | Presents a persistent vertex after its adjacent local cells. | Precedes destruction when the transition removes the vertex.
touchHangingFaceLastTime | Finishes one hanging-face use. | Follows the adjacent cell event.
touchHangingVertexLastTime | Finishes one hanging-vertex use. | Follows adjacent face and cell events.
destroyCell | Releases data of a removed cell. | Follows its last touch and precedes destruction of adjacent faces and vertices.
destroyFace | Releases data of a removed face. | Follows its last touch.
destroyVertex | Releases data of a removed persistent vertex. | Follows its last touch and adjacent destruction events.
endTraversal | Finishes one observer clone. | Follows every entity event of that observer.
unprepareTraversal | Finalises rank-wide action-set state. | Runs after every observer clone has been destroyed.

Creation and destruction callbacks occur during creational or regrid
transition sweeps. Standing sweeps emit first-touch and last-touch events only.

# Markers and data

Entity records do not carry their geometric or ownership context. Generated
callbacks receive a marker that derives this information from the traversal
event:

- peano4::dataview::VertexMarker
- peano4::dataview::FaceMarker
- peano4::dataview::CellMarker

Markers provide coordinates, mesh width, selection within the adjacent entity
set, hanging state, refinement state, and local ownership. Debug coordinates
stored inside generated data records are diagnostic fields and are not an
application interface.

Generated observers translate the event's pool slots into references to the
cell, face, and vertex data used by an action set. Interface transfers call
the generated merge routines with peano4::grid::SendReceiveContext::InterRank,
peano4::grid::SendReceiveContext::IntraRank or
peano4::grid::SendReceiveContext::Consolidation.

# Coarse-grid data

Callbacks in the first level below a subtree-task root receive synthetic parent
storage. Deeper callbacks receive the physical parent data of the next coarser
level. An action set that requires the physical parent performs that operation
away from the task boundary.

# Action-set order

An algorithmic step maps to one generated
peano4::grid::GridTraversalObserver. Its action sets are ordered by
`descend_invocation_order` for events that descend into the tree. The reverse
order is used where the generated observer unwinds the traversal. This order
controls action sets that touch the same entity; it does not order independent
subtree tasks.

*/
